                            <comment id="497515" author="JIRAUSER18417" created="Wed, 8 Jul 2026 19:03:46 +0000">&lt;p&gt;We hit the same issue. Independently root-caused it to the same line — the posix_acl_dup() in the ACL_TYPE_DEFAULT branch of ll_get_inode_acl(). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Validated on kernel 6.8.0-1060-aws.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before fix: ~1 leaked posix_acl per directory per default-ACL access (unreclaimable). &lt;br/&gt;
After fix: zero leaked posix_acl remaining&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This was introduced by the backport of &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254 &lt;/a&gt;specifically in &lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;acl.c&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;(&lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254/11/lustre/llite/acl.c)" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254/11/lustre/llite/acl.c)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sebastien" class="user-hover" rel="sebastien"&gt;sebastien&lt;/a&gt; since this was introduced from &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/56254&lt;/a&gt; do you have concern with this fix?&lt;/p&gt;

